      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The lake’s water level can rise up to 11 feet overnight during extreme floods, a record set during a single night of heavy rain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://alamo.lakesonline.com/Default.asp",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Alamo Lake State Park sits at 1,104 feet above sea level, offering crystal‑clear water surrounded by mountains, wildflowers, and cacti.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://azstateparks.com/alamo-lake/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wildlife watchers often spot bald or golden eagles, mule deer, and even wild burros roaming the park’s shoreline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://azstateparks.com/alamo-lake/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Stargazers enjoy clear night skies because the nearest city lights are about 40 miles away, making the Milky Way visible.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
